# US Social Security number structure, using SSA's invalid-number rules:
# https://www.ssa.gov/employer/randomizationfaqs.html
# Accepts either nine digits or the consistent three-two-four hyphenated form.
# Does not verify issuance, ownership, or identity; no external lookup is made.
# Leading/trailing spaces, partial hyphenation, and non-ASCII digits are rejected.
# Use verbose mode and full matching, as configured in rule.ini.

# First three digits cannot be 000, 666, or 900-999.
(?! 000 | 666 | 9[0-9]{2} ) [0-9]{3}

# Capture either a hyphen or an empty separator; reuse it below.
(?P<separator> -? )

# Middle two digits cannot both be zero.
(?! 00 ) [0-9]{2}
(?P=separator)

# Final four digits cannot all be zero.
(?! 0000 ) [0-9]{4}
